      "name": "Filth Fever",
      "actions": null,
      "traits": [
        "disease"
      ],
      "description": "<p>The sickened and unconscious conditions from filth fever can't end or be reduced until the disease is cured</p>\n<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 14 Fortitude save</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Stage 1</strong> carrier with no ill effect (<span class=\"roll\" onclick=\"roll(this)\">1d4</span> hours)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Sickened 1 (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 3</strong> sickened 1 and Slowed 1 (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Unconscious (1 day)</p>\n<p><strong>Stage 5</strong> dead</p>",
      "collapsed": false
    }
  ],
  "spellcastingEntries": [],
  "description": "<p>At around 5 feet long, this massive, rotting serpent lacks potent venom, but its bite still injects putrid fluid that can cause infection.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Simple to create and varied in purpose, these shambling undead are often used for their strength and endless stamina to conduct boring, repetitive tasks.</p>",
